  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the sum of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities), which in this case leads to preferring Lottery A due to its higher maximum outcome. The individual also ends up favoring the higher amount (2500 over 2400), motivated by the perception that the probabilities are almost identical. While the individual does not explicitly sum all outcomes or describe a rule that ignores probabilities entirely, their reasoning effectively reduces the choice to a comparison of the highest possible outcomes under near-equal chance. This aligns closely with the core logic of the decision reason—disregarding small probability differences and focusing on outcome magnitude. However, the verbal report emphasizes subjective equivalence of probabilities rather than a general rule of summing outcomes regardless of probability. Therefore, while the reasoning leads to the same conclusion and shares conceptual similarity, the exact cognitive process described does not fully match the formal structure of the decision reason. The match is strong but not certain.",
  "final_assessment_score": 75
}

